    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d690">

                <pb facs="0739" n="727" sameAs="frus:frus1945v04/pg727"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 EW/4–745: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-04-26T20:00:00-04:00">April 26, 1945—8
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1700. Your 1719, April 7. British Embassy advises that Steel<anchor n="9"
                        xml:id="d690-f1"/> has been instructed to impress on SHAEF<anchor n="10"
                        xml:id="d690-f2"/> the importance which the British Government attaches to
                    the political aspect of the employment of French troops in Italian territory.
                    While feeling that in view of Bidault’s assurances the Italians are unduly
                    apprehensive, the British Government welcomes SACMED’s<anchor n="11"
                        xml:id="d690-f3"/> proposal (Caserta’s 60, April 2<anchor n="12"
                        xml:id="d690-f4"/>) to request SCAEF<anchor n="13" xml:id="d690-f5"/> to
                    withdraw French troops as soon as possible after the Germans cease fighting or
                    French troops are no longer needed. It adds that undoubtedly SCAEF will take
                    special care that French troops not be in a position to engage in independent
                    activities.</p>
                <p>Please make similar representation to SHAEF on behalf of this Government through
                    your liaison.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
